      "section": "Running enrichment",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Three panels share one rank axis. The top one walks the enrichment score along the ranked gene list, stepping up at every set member and down at every other gene, so it leaves zero and comes back to it at the last rank; its extremum is the enrichment score. The middle rug marks where the members actually sit. The bottom panel is the metric the list was ranked by. Shaded is the leading edge \u2014 the stretch between the extremum and the enriched end of the list, the members carrying the signal. A set with no signal wanders near zero.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
